<title>GERMANY: Summary of Ifo April German business survey.</title>
<headline>Summary of Ifo April German business survey.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following is a summary of key points in the IFO economic research institute's monthly business survey for April (sectors are west German unless</p>
<p>otherwise stated, comparisons are against pvs month):</p>
<p>Ifo said last week that its west German climate index -- the most closely watched of its business barometers -- rose in April</p>
<p>to 94.7 from 92.6 in March.</p>
<p>MANUFACTURING INDUSTRY (EXCL FOOD, LUXURY GOODS):</p>
<p>Current business - less unhappy</p>
<p>Business outlook - still optimistic</p>
<p>Incoming orders - lively</p>
<p>Orders levels - higher</p>
<p>Export outlook - confident</p>
<p>Production plans - slower expansion</p>
<p>SEMI-MANUFACTURED GOODS:</p>
<p>Current business - better</p>
<p>Business outlook - better</p>
<p>Orders level - improved</p>
<p>Export outlook - slightly less optimistic</p>
<p>Production plans - more moderate growth</p>
<p>Note - In chemicals situation good but export outlook less</p>
<p>bright; metals -- strong demand, order books up; pulp and paper</p>
<p>-- little change expected to satisfactory situation; textiles --</p>
<p>fears of falling production and exports.</p>
<p>CAPITAL GOODS:</p>
<p>Current business - bad, despite strong demand</p>
<p>Business outlook - low expectations</p>
<p>Orders level - not high enough</p>
<p>Export outlook - confident</p>
<p>Production plans - low expectations</p>
<p>Note - In machine-building situation less unfavourable;</p>
<p>electricals -- looking to exports; vehicles -- no more</p>
<p>optimistic; precision mechanical/optical sector -- less</p>
<p>pessimistic.</p>
<p>CONSUMER DURABLES:</p>
<p>Current business - mainly good</p>
<p>Business outlook - positive</p>
<p>Orders level - improved</p>
<p>Export outlook - not so optimistic</p>
<p>Production plans - expansive</p>
<p>Note - Carmakers expect to expand output; electronics -- sceptical; precision mechanical/optical -- less gloomy.</p>
<p>CONSUMER GOODS:</p>
<p>Current business - again better, but still mainly negative</p>
<p>Business outlook - worse</p>
<p>Export outlook - hopeful</p>
<p>Note - Clothing sector no recovery; shoes -- more sceptical.</p>
<p>CONSTRUCTION:</p>
<p>Current business - no less gloomy</p>
<p>Business outlook - very pessimistic</p>
<p>Production plans - no recovery seen</p>
<p>Orders level - 2.6 months of output, just up on year earlier</p>
<p>Prices - still falling</p>
<p>Personnel plans - job cuts to continue</p>
<p>WHOLESALE TRADE:</p>
<p>Current business - slightly better, but still negative</p>
<p>Business outlook - sceptical</p>
<p>RETAIL TRADE:</p>
<p>Current business - better, still negative</p>
<p>Business outlook - sceptical</p>
<p>Orders level - shrinking</p>
<p>Prices - calm</p>
<p>EAST GERMAN MANUFACTURING INDUSTRY</p>
<p>Current business - unchanged, almost satisfactory</p>
<p>Business outlook - less optimistic</p>
<p>Export outlook - less hopeful</p>
<p>Orders level - unchanged</p>
<p>Production plans - less dynamic</p>
<p>Personnel plans - job losses to slow</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
